  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The price of gold produced by state-owned mining company Antam has experienced a decline in the Indonesian market. According to recent reports, the price dropped by Rp5,000, bringing the cost per gram down to Rp2,495,000 from the previous level of Rp2,500,000. Additionally, the buyback price—the rate at which the company repurchases gold from customers—decreased by Rp50,000, settling at Rp2,090,000 per gram. These fluctuations are monitored through the official Logam Mulia website and reflect broader market trends concerning precious metals in Indonesia. While this decline is specific to current Antam listings, other segments of the national economy are seeing varied price shifts, such as changes in basic food commodities. The gold market continues to be a subject of public attention as analysts and investors track these ongoing price adjustments across the country.",
